 GAMING CAFE LAN SETUP - 10 PCs

 STEP 1: CHOOSE THE CABLE

Cable Type: Cat6 Ethernet Cable

I would choose Cat6 Ethernet cables to connect all
10 gaming PCs in the cafe.

STEP 2: CONSIDER SPEED

Cat6 Ethernet provides enough speed for LAN gaming
and supports fast communication between the PCs.

 STEP 3: CONSIDER DISTANCE

A gaming cafe normally has short distances between
the PCs, switch and other network devices.

Ethernet is suitable for these short-distance
connections.

 STEP 4: CONSIDER BUDGET

Ethernet cables are cheaper and easier to install
than fiber optic cables.

This makes Ethernet a practical choice for a
10-PC gaming cafe.

STEP 5: CHOOSE THE TOOL

Tool: RJ45 Crimper

I would use an RJ45 crimper to attach RJ45 connectors
to the ends of the Cat6 Ethernet cables.

STEP 6: WHY NOT FIBER OPTICS?

Fiber optic cables are mainly useful for long-distance
and high-speed network connections.

For a small gaming cafe, fiber optics would add
extra cost and installation complexity.

FINAL CHOICE

Cable : Cat6 Ethernet
Tool  : RJ45 Crimper

Main Reasons:

* Good speed
* Suitable for short distances
* Lower cost
* Easy installation
* Easy maintenance
